    74	## 3. Cells and execution contract
    75	
    76	- **Churn model.** Each of the nine honest opponents plays honest-max delivery and offer and, in each round, retires its
    77	  identity and re-enters under a fresh one with probability p (`docs/revision/churn/churn_v2.py` `HonestChurn`). The draw
    78	  uses the episode's `policy_seed[t, e]`, so it is deterministic and the same for every rule on the same seed. The model
    79	  keeps provider capacity and quality fixed and changes identity age; it also resets an honest provider's history and
    80	  lets it leave a false ban, so it does not isolate age information alone. **Rates p in {0.01, 0.05}** are illustrative
    81	  sensitivity settings without empirical calibration: mean identity lifetimes of 100 and 20 rounds, about 18 and 89
    82	  honest replacements per episode (measured, section 1). Whether the focal identity stays the newest is measured (section 4).
    83	- **Cells.** {R3, C*, B3} x fresh0..fresh5 x {0.01, 0.05} at rho 0.2, D2+H3, registered search budget (5 restarts, 300
    84	  evaluations, 5 training seeds), the market's 200 evaluation seeds, a doubling check with its held-out evaluation on
    85	  every cell: **36 cells**, plus the gate cell.
    86	- **Driver.** `docs/revision/churn/churn_v2.py` (under `docs/`: the code freeze allows changes only there). It runs the
    87	  frozen `revision_v2` stage functions through `_run_one` and reuses the reset driver's helpers
    88	  (`docs/revision/followup/reset_followup_v2.py`: input copies, pre-episode checks, follow-up freeze, acceptance,
