    90	  `train_cell` (which `eval_cell` calls), so search, twin search, the doubling stage's reference menu, and evaluation run
    91	  under churn; `select_reference`, so a cell with churning opponents never reuses a candidate's stored no-churn training
    92	  profits (only the abstain candidate, whose profit is zero, keeps its value); and `reference_of`, so a churn job's
    93	  frozen reference carries its training-seed score evaluated under the same churn, which the doubling stage's
    94	  `reference_change` subtracts. Churn job ids carry the suffix `|churn<p>` so they never overwrite the copied registered
    95	  D2+H3 records that the reference menus read; each rate writes to its own directory (`results/v2/followup-churn/p<p>/`),
    96	  never to `eval/all`.
    97	- **References: frozen candidate, played under churn.** Each (market, rule) keeps its frozen truthful reference
    98	  candidate. Two reselections are distinguished. Reselecting among the frozen menu's candidates under churn needs only
    99	  their evaluation on the training seeds; the doubling stage does it for every cell (with the fix above), and its
   100	  `reference_change` is reported as a diagnostic, not as a bound on held-out bias. Regenerating the menus under churn
   101	  would need 60 D2+H3 and 60 X7-SC searches per rate, about 12.19 USD per rate before the churn slowdown (section 9); it
   102	  is not done.
   103	- **Checks before any episode** (reset driver, plan draft 5): configuration hash equals the container hash; salt; known
   104	  commit; runner and `sim/` equal protocol-v2; each job's runner, salt, configuration, root, seeds, rule parameters and
   105	  context equal its frozen reference's provenance; output not inside `--src` or `eval/all`. Inputs are copied read-only
   106	  and hash-checked against the original records and freeze; the follow-up freeze and acceptance run before evaluation
   107	  and doubling; a final inventory records every output hash, the environment, and the churn driver's hash.
   108	- **Validation before spend (free, on the Mac).** (a) Unit tests: the churn policy is truthful and exits at rate p,
   109	  deterministically; p = 0 never exits; the wrapper adds churning opponents to training and evaluation cells, also in
   110	  pool workers, and leaves other jobs unchanged; churn ids and provenance are distinct; under churn every menu candidate
   111	  is rerun on the five training seeds and the frozen reference's score is recomputed; newcomer counts, unavailable
