   122	  that saved gate record: passing, for this cell and id mapping, and run by the same driver version (its hash in the
   123	  gate's inventory); production runs cannot skip the gate.
   124	
   125	## 4. Diagnostics (evaluation only, no search)
   126	
   127	For every cell, the base and the doubled winner are rerun on the evaluation seeds under churn (`diagnostics` stage):
   128	per-seed normalised profits; per episode the [served, audited] counts by identity age, in bins [0, 10), [10, 20),
   129	[20, 50), [50, 200), for honest replacement identities, honest initial identities, and the focal provider's identities;
   130	honest replacements per episode; and per episode two "newest" shares for the focal identity. (i) Creation-time newest:
   131	the share of rounds in which its creation round is strictly the latest among all current identities; this is not the
   132	order R3 uses. (ii) Mechanism-relevant: over the rounds in which it holds assigned jobs, the share in which its
   133	first-offer round is strictly the latest among the identities holding assigned jobs, which is how R3 ages and ranks
   134	identities (`sim/mechanisms/factorial.py`). Only (ii) is used to discuss R3's targeting.
   135	A bin with no served job is reported as unavailable. Pooling over markets: per rule, winner and bin, the mean of the
   136	market shares over the markets where the share is available, with that count. A higher audited share of honest
   137	newcomers is greater audit exposure; it is not by itself a financial loss.
   138	
   139	## 5. Analysis (fixed now)
   140	
   141	- Per market and pooled g_p(r), d_p, q_p, with paired seed bootstrap intervals (9,999 resamples, percentile, 95 percent;
   142	  the same resampled seed indices for every rule and rate of a market; pooled replicates resample seeds within each
   143	  market and average the six market means). The intervals condition on the six markets and the selected policies; they
   144	  do not include search uncertainty or uncertainty across markets.
   145	- Changes from no churn, paired by seed with the registered records: base with base, doubled with doubled.
   146	- Attack and reference profit terms separately; the reselection diagnostic per cell; sign counts over the six markets.
   147	- No confirmatory test, no multiplicity family, no change to any registered decision; all results are labelled
