   149	
   150	## 6. Pre-specified expectations
   151	
   152	Written after the disclosed peek in section 1 and before any churn search. Scored on point estimates, as met (holds
   153	under both the base and the doubled searches, each against its own no-churn baseline), failed (fails under both), or not
   154	established (the two disagree).
   155	
   156	1. Pooled g_0.05(R3) exceeds the registered pooled no-churn g(R3) (base 0.0649; doubled against the doubled value).
   157	2. Pooled d_0.05 = C* - R3 is below the registered no-churn value (base 0.0207; doubled 0.0296).
   158	3. q_0.01 = B3 - R3 is positive on all six markets.
   159	4. At p = 0.05, the market-pooled audited share of honest replacement identities in their first ten rounds is higher
   160	   under R3 than under C* and than under B3, for both winners (a cross-rule difference under churn; no no-churn baseline
   161	   exists for honest replacement identities in these cells).
   162	
   163	A failure is not read as evidence of a particular cause. Only if expectation 2 is met may the paper say that R3's
   164	measured edge over C* shrinks when honest opponents churn; only if 4 is met that, under churn, R3 exposes honest newcomers
   165	to more audits than C* and B3 do.
